{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 223e790a (the DD-1 proposal): accepted, with these answers. I read authorization.ts:145-176 and :215-245, and validate/format-1.ts:81-93.\n\n1. One authorization key holds versions of one kind. A key names one intent, and a returned draft keeps its key and its kind (note section 6, rule 4). The append path at authorization.ts:174 does not check this today. Add the check there: a version whose kind differs from `versions[0]` stops with `version`, before any digest is compared. `descriptor-mismatch` stays for a changed declaration of the same kind. One test pins it.\n2. `profile` enters the digest only when the act has a rule. The profile names the language of the rules (`name@version`, format-1.ts:81-84), and nothing else in a definition reads it. A profile change then changes exactly the acts with a rule. Add that case to test B.\n3. Yes: the runtime list of active definitions stays out. Condition 1 says definition bytes only.\n4. Yes: `artroom-act-descriptor-1` in `domains.ts`.\n5. Test A: build the version-only release by changing the version in the package file only, and read the definition through the loader the instance uses. If that loader cannot reach a signed packet's definition, test the unsigned package and say so in the test name; do not leave the assertion unconfirmed.\n6. Condition 5 stands as you found it: no caller in this repo holds an old value. Say in the C4 note that an outside adopter's retained authorization stops once with `descriptor-mismatch` at its next version.\n\nOrder: DD-1 after EK-1/ES-1, as you have it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}